<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson to sell modems to Enator Dotcom.</title>
<headline>Ericsson to sell modems to Enator Dotcom.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group AB LM Ericsson said on Tuesday it won an order to sell base band modems to Enator Dotcom's new city network in Lulea, northern Sweden.  </p>
<p>&quot;The deal in Lulea is just the start of Ericsson's breakthrough on the market for base band modems,&quot; Ericsson said in a statement</p>
<p>&quot;Base band modems are an important part of our focus on products for network access.&quot;</p>
<p>The company did not disclose the value of the deal.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
